/P 208 0 R
/E (Our research group pioneered micro-pixel silicon detectors, first introduced in 1993 and now known as MAPD \(Micro-pixel Avalanche Photodiodes\) or SiPM \(Silicon Photomultipliers\). These solid-state sensors have largely replaced traditional photomultiplier tubes due to their compactness, robustness, low operating voltage, magnetic-field immunity, and compatibility with modern electronics.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [1]
>>
