/E ( Overall, this study fills a critical methodological gap by integrating a memory-type estimation mechanism into systematic sampling. The findings highlight the practical advantages of incorporating exponentially weighted historical information in improving finite population mean estimation. The proposed estimator is especially relevant in structured data environments, such as environmental monitoring, agricultural surveys, market research, and official statistics, where systematic sampling is routinely applied. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [4]
>>
